# tags-guard — an information-flow reservation (specification v0.6).
#
# A cross-border transfer is reserved to the Data Protection Officer only when the
# token carries the declared, non-id tag `non_eu` (cf. GDPR Art. 44-49). The tag is
# a declared data-flow category tested by membership — not a computed value, and not
# a branch on identity. A token tagged `non_eu` -> reserved -> withheld pending the
# DPO; an otherwise-identical token without it is unreserved -> auto -> released.
#
# Which tags exist and what they trigger is policy, not language (specification §10).
actor pipeline
human dpo role dpo
gate transfer risk high grant pipeline
reserve cross_border by dpo when tags contains non_eu
cord pipeline -> transfer
cord transfer -> master
